---
# skip_list rationale:
# - var-naming[no-role-prefix]: stortree deliberately uses one flat
#   `stortree_*` namespace for facts/defaults shared *across* roles
#   (the `stortree` fact itself, path defaults in stortree_facts,
#   stortree_root/user/group in stortree_common, ...) rather than
#   role-private variables -- that's the point of the shared contract
#   described in docs/spec.md §1, not an oversight.
#
# - ignore-errors: the directory-creation tasks in stortree_mounts run
#   against paths that may sit under an already-mounted-but-unreachable
#   rclone mount, where root itself gets EACCES and there is nothing to
#   correct until that mount is replaced later in the same run (see that
#   file's header comment and stortree_path_masked()). The suggested
#   `failed_when` can't express this: the condition isn't a recognizable
#   message but "this path is currently behind a FUSE mount presenting
#   an ownership this host can't see through", which is exactly what the
#   task would have to succeed at to evaluate. Failing the play there
#   would abort every *later* task, including the ones that fix it.
#
# - no-handler: the three "Restart any ... whose unit file actually
#   changed" tasks in stortree_mounts loop over a `register`ed template
#   result and restart only the units whose own file re-rendered. A
#   handler is notified once for the whole loop and has no access to
#   which iterations changed, so the handler form would restart every
#   resolved mount on any change -- disrupting open file handles on
#   unrelated mounts, which is the specific thing these tasks are
#   scoped to avoid.
skip_list:
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
  - ignore-errors
  - no-handler
